Web Platform Tests, cookies/http-state/resources/test-files at commit
e2c77fa4d187c6a179f9343925ef9c3ab5488e86 (the last commit before the cases were rewritten into
server-driven tests), files not prefixed `disabled-`. Originally Adam Barth's http-state test
suite (RFC 6265), maintained in WPT to match browser behaviour.

Each `<name>-test` holds the response headers for http://home.example.org:8888/cookie-parser?<name>
(`Set-Cookie` lines, and an optional `Location` naming the URL to read cookies for; default
http://home.example.org:8888/cookie-parser-result?<name>). `<name>-expected` holds the `Cookie`
header expected for that URL, or nothing.

